WEBVTT

00:00:13.444 --> 00:00:14.625
It's not a dream.

00:00:14.744 --> 00:00:16.726
You ever heard of an
out-Of-Body experience?

00:00:16.762 --> 00:00:18.225
We're spirits...

00:00:19.253 --> 00:00:20.640
Of people close to death.

00:00:22.678 --> 00:00:25.625
Your son is dying, and
you're worried about the colt?

00:00:27.016 --> 00:00:29.118
You shoot me in the heart, son!

00:00:31.141 --> 00:00:32.505
You're bringing the
demon here, aren't you?

00:00:32.506 --> 00:00:34.969
Having some stupid, macho showdown!

00:00:35.581 --> 00:00:37.790
If you killed that damn
thing when you had the chance,

00:00:37.801 --> 00:00:39.928
None of this would have happened.

00:00:46.775 --> 00:00:48.333
I want to make a deal.

00:00:49.941 --> 00:00:52.069
You're much prettier than
the last reaper I met.

00:00:52.075 --> 00:00:55.538
I will give you the colt and the
bullet. But you got to help Dean.

00:00:56.933 --> 00:00:58.613
So, we have a deal?

00:00:59.189 --> 00:01:01.418
You still need to sweeten the pot.

00:01:03.787 --> 00:01:05.746
Today is your lucky day, kid.

00:01:08.015 --> 00:01:10.096
You watch out for Sammy, okay?

00:01:18.507 --> 00:01:19.543
Okay.

00:01:19.931 --> 00:01:20.837
Dad?

00:01:24.739 --> 00:01:26.708
Time of death, 10:41 a.M.

00:01:53.195 --> 00:01:55.837
God, I hate clowns. Always creep me out.

00:01:55.842 --> 00:01:57.400
Shh! She likes them.

00:02:06.943 --> 00:02:08.231
Last ride, Nora.

00:02:22.176 --> 00:02:23.851
Look, mom, another clown.

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:31.477
What are you trying to
do, scare your father?

00:02:31.483 --> 00:02:32.480
Honey.

00:02:48.797 --> 00:02:50.557
Look, mom, a clown.

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:56.928
You missed him.

00:04:50.579 --> 00:04:52.319
Before he...

00:04:53.435 --> 00:04:54.522
Before he...

00:04:59.447 --> 00:05:01.025
Did he say anything to you?

00:05:03.598 --> 00:05:05.064
About anything?

00:05:12.645 --> 00:05:14.243
No.

00:05:18.235 --> 00:05:19.564
Nothing.

00:05:58.915 --> 00:06:00.354
How's the car coming along?

00:06:00.361 --> 00:06:01.287
Slow.

00:06:02.324 --> 00:06:03.241
Yeah?

00:06:04.549 --> 00:06:06.335
You need any help?

00:06:06.343 --> 00:06:07.891
What? You under a hood?

00:06:08.456 --> 00:06:09.635
I'll pass.

00:06:12.215 --> 00:06:13.412
Need anything else, then?

00:06:15.922 --> 00:06:17.009
Stop it, Sam.

00:06:17.813 --> 00:06:18.661
Stop what?

00:06:18.668 --> 00:06:19.995
Stop asking if I need anything.

00:06:20.010 --> 00:06:22.469
Stop asking if I'm okay. I'm okay.

00:06:22.835 --> 00:06:24.784
Really. I promise.

00:06:28.616 --> 00:06:30.316
All right, Dean, it's just...

00:06:31.622 --> 00:06:34.852
We've been at Bobby's for over a week
now, and you haven't brought up dad once.

00:06:36.522 --> 00:06:37.948
You know what? You're right.

00:06:39.048 --> 00:06:39.984
Come here.

00:06:40.419 --> 00:06:42.297
I'm gonna lay my head
gently on your shoulder.

00:06:42.453 --> 00:06:44.704
Maybe we could cry, hug,

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:47.218
Maybe even slow dance.
Don't patronize me, Dean.

00:06:47.223 --> 00:06:50.654
Dad is dead, the colt is gone,
and it seems pretty damn likely

00:06:50.660 --> 00:06:53.301
That the demon is behind all of this.
And you're acting like nothing happened.

00:06:53.306 --> 00:06:54.754
What do you want me to say?
Say something, all right?!

00:06:54.758 --> 00:06:58.041
Hell, say anything! Aren't you
angry? Don't you want revenge?

00:06:58.284 --> 00:07:01.656
But all you do is sit out here all day
long buried underneath this damn car.

00:07:01.661 --> 00:07:03.660
Revenge, huh? Sounds good. Yeah!

00:07:04.269 --> 00:07:06.158
Got any leads on where the demon is?

00:07:06.161 --> 00:07:08.940
Making heads or tails of any of
dad's research? 'Cause I sure ain't.

00:07:08.945 --> 00:07:10.606
You know, when we do finally find it...

00:07:10.611 --> 00:07:11.676
Oh,

00:07:11.684 --> 00:07:13.633
No, wait, like you
said, the colt's gone.

00:07:13.636 --> 00:07:15.515
But I'm sure you figured
out another way to kill it.

00:07:15.691 --> 00:07:18.008
We've got nothing, Sam. Nothing, okay?

00:07:18.013 --> 00:07:20.866
The only thing I can do
is I can work on the car.

00:07:23.044 --> 00:07:24.712
Well, we got something, all right?

00:07:25.601 --> 00:07:27.228
It's what I came out here to tell you.

00:07:27.234 --> 00:07:28.701
It's one of dad's old phones.

00:07:28.705 --> 00:07:31.987
It took me a while, but I cracked
his voice mail code. Listen to this.

00:07:36.071 --> 00:07:38.162
<i>John, it's Ellen... Again.</i>

00:07:38.445 --> 00:07:41.235
<i>Look, don't be stubborn. You
know I can help you. Call me.</i>

00:07:42.674 --> 00:07:44.321
That message is four months old.

00:07:44.328 --> 00:07:46.115
Dad saved that chick's
message for four months?

00:07:46.119 --> 00:07:47.358
Yeah. Who's Ellen?

00:07:47.365 --> 00:07:49.032
Any mention of her in dad's journal? No,

00:07:49.036 --> 00:07:51.585
But I ran a trace on the
number, and I got an address.

00:07:54.369 --> 00:07:56.167
Ask Bobby if we can use one of his cars.

00:08:07.756 --> 00:08:09.472
This is humiliating.

00:08:13.317 --> 00:08:15.514
I feel like a friggin' soccer mom.

00:08:15.518 --> 00:08:17.808
It's the only car Bobby had running.

00:08:20.792 --> 00:08:22.146
H ello?

00:08:24.166 --> 00:08:25.926
Anybody here? Alright.

00:08:25.931 --> 00:08:28.150
Hey, did you bring the... Of course.

00:08:57.483 --> 00:08:58.812
Hey, buddy?

00:09:02.754 --> 00:09:05.255
I'm guessing that isn't Ellen. Yeah.

00:09:23.286 --> 00:09:25.415
Oh, god, please let that be a rifle.

00:09:26.172 --> 00:09:27.999
No, I'm just real happy to see you.

00:09:28.695 --> 00:09:30.874
Don't move. Not moving. Copy that.

00:09:32.395 --> 00:09:33.871
You should know something, miss.

00:09:33.946 --> 00:09:35.634
When you put a rifle on someone,

00:09:35.638 --> 00:09:37.738
You don't want to put it
right against their back,

00:09:37.943 --> 00:09:40.125
'Cause it makes it real easy to do...

00:09:42.874 --> 00:09:43.902
That!

00:09:44.969 --> 00:09:45.927
Sam!

00:09:46.320 --> 00:09:47.677
I need some help in here.

00:09:47.684 --> 00:09:49.303
I can't see. I can't even see!

00:09:49.459 --> 00:09:50.533
Sorry, Dean.

00:09:51.239 --> 00:09:53.131
I can't right now. I'm a...

00:09:53.656 --> 00:09:55.025
Little  tied up.

00:09:57.742 --> 00:09:59.062
Sam? Dean?

00:10:01.069 --> 00:10:02.159
Winchester?

00:10:03.395 --> 00:10:04.231
Yeah.

00:10:05.140 --> 00:10:06.296
Son of a bitch.

00:10:06.300 --> 00:10:07.589
Mom, you know these guys?

00:10:07.595 --> 00:10:09.922
Yeah,  I think these are
John Winchester's boys.

00:10:13.343 --> 00:10:14.311
Hey, I'm Ellen.

00:10:14.759 --> 00:10:16.017
That's my daughter, Jo.

00:10:17.231 --> 00:10:18.058
Hey.

00:10:18.605 --> 00:10:20.035
You're not gonna hit me again, are you?

00:10:21.212 --> 00:10:22.276
Here you go.

00:10:22.284 --> 00:10:23.230
Thanks.

00:10:26.540 --> 00:10:28.391
You called our dad, said you could help.

00:10:29.026 --> 00:10:30.144
Help with what?

00:10:31.439 --> 00:10:32.957
Well,

00:10:33.116 --> 00:10:34.523
The demon, of course.

00:10:36.361 --> 00:10:37.960
I heard he was closing in on it.

00:10:39.047 --> 00:10:41.588
Was there an article in "the demon
hunter's quarterly" that I missed?

00:10:41.592 --> 00:10:43.249
I mean, who are you? How
do you know about all this?

00:10:43.253 --> 00:10:44.884
Hey, I just run a saloon.

00:10:45.500 --> 00:10:49.002
But hunters have been known
to pass through now and again,

00:10:49.118 --> 00:10:51.147
Including your dad a long time ago.

00:10:51.161 --> 00:10:52.730
John was like family once. Oh yeah?

00:10:52.732 --> 00:10:54.532
I mean he's never mentioned you before.

00:10:55.540 --> 00:10:57.456
You'd have to ask him that.

00:11:00.309 --> 00:11:01.998
So, why exactly do we need your help?

00:11:02.002 --> 00:11:03.829
Hey, don't do me any favors.

00:11:04.146 --> 00:11:05.784
Look, if you don't want my help, fine.

00:11:05.789 --> 00:11:07.820
Don't let the door smack
your ass on the way out.

00:11:07.978 --> 00:11:09.645
But John wouldn't have sent you if...

00:11:15.711 --> 00:11:16.845
He didn't send you.

00:11:23.454 --> 00:11:24.696
He's all right, isn't he?

00:11:26.510 --> 00:11:27.388
No.

00:11:28.874 --> 00:11:29.881
No, he isn't.

00:11:30.269 --> 00:11:32.337
It was the demon, we think.

00:11:33.366 --> 00:11:35.845
It just got him before
he got it, I guess.

00:11:39.689 --> 00:11:41.618
I'm so sorry. It's okay.

00:11:41.843 --> 00:11:43.111
We're all right.

00:11:43.293 --> 00:11:45.245
Really, I know how
close you and your dad...

00:11:45.247 --> 00:11:46.676
Really, lady, I'm fine.

00:11:50.748 --> 00:11:52.909
So, look, if you can help...

00:11:54.186 --> 00:11:56.307
We could use all the help we can get.

00:11:56.682 --> 00:11:58.108
Well, we can't.

00:11:59.417 --> 00:12:00.696
But Ash will.

00:12:00.701 --> 00:12:02.638
Who's Ash? Ash!

00:12:04.425 --> 00:12:05.563
What?

00:12:07.541 --> 00:12:09.162
Closing time?

00:12:11.329 --> 00:12:12.568
That's Ash?

00:12:13.555 --> 00:12:14.573
He's a genius.

00:12:17.431 --> 00:12:19.570
You got to be kidding
me. This guy's no genius.

00:12:19.575 --> 00:12:21.427
He's a Lynyrd Skynyrd roadie.

00:12:21.943 --> 00:12:24.181
I like you. Thanks.

00:12:24.367 --> 00:12:25.653
Just give him a chance.

00:12:30.558 --> 00:12:31.574
All right.

00:12:33.005 --> 00:12:36.304
Well, this stuff's about a
year's worth of our dad's work. So

00:12:37.171 --> 00:12:38.570
Let's see what you make of it.

00:12:49.468 --> 00:12:54.472
Come on. This crap ain't real. Ain't
nobody can track a demon like this.

00:12:58.543 --> 00:12:59.753
Our dad could.

00:13:02.775 --> 00:13:05.263
These are nonparametric
statistical overviews,

00:13:05.267 --> 00:13:08.310
Cross-Spectrum correlations. I mean...

00:13:09.024 --> 00:13:10.123
Damn!

00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:13.160
They're signs,

00:13:13.683 --> 00:13:17.235
Omens. If you can track them,
you can track this demon.

00:13:17.242 --> 00:13:21.184
You know, like crop
failures, electrical storms.

00:13:21.190 --> 00:13:25.123
You ever been struck by
lightning? It ain't fun.

00:13:25.126 --> 00:13:29.081
Can you track it or not?
Yeah, with this, I think so.

00:13:29.096 --> 00:13:32.175
But it's gonna take time. Give me...

00:13:34.014 --> 00:13:36.156
51 hours.

00:13:42.122 --> 00:13:43.468
Hey, man! Yeah?

00:13:43.483 --> 00:13:45.935
By the way, I dig the haircut.

00:13:47.130 --> 00:13:49.209
All business up front,

00:13:49.345 --> 00:13:51.014
Party in the back.

00:14:04.037 --> 00:14:05.492
Hey, Ellen, what is that?

00:14:06.619 --> 00:14:08.088
It's a police scanner.

00:14:08.094 --> 00:14:12.749
We keep tabs on things. No,
no, no, no. The... folder.

00:14:20.569 --> 00:14:23.077
I was gonna give this
to a friend of mine, but

00:14:23.984 --> 00:14:24.732
Take a look

00:14:24.738 --> 00:14:25.644
If you want.

00:14:27.442 --> 00:14:28.157
Thanks.

00:14:29.568 --> 00:14:31.537
How did your mom get
into this stuff, anyway?

00:14:31.542 --> 00:14:32.536
My dad.

00:14:32.773 --> 00:14:33.851
He was a hunter.

00:14:35.268 --> 00:14:36.506
He passed away.

00:14:38.262 --> 00:14:39.259
I'm sorry.

00:14:39.718 --> 00:14:40.915
It was a long time ago.

00:14:41.411 --> 00:14:42.577
I was just a kid.

00:14:44.598 --> 00:14:45.975
Sorry to hear about yo dad.

00:14:48.005 --> 00:14:48.848
Yeah.

00:14:51.879 --> 00:14:52.617
So,

00:14:53.763 --> 00:14:56.175
I guess I got 51 hours to waste.

00:14:56.471 --> 00:14:58.158
Maybe tonight we should...

00:15:04.677 --> 00:15:06.266
Oh, you know what? Never mind.

00:15:06.970 --> 00:15:09.372
What? Nothing, just...

00:15:10.800 --> 00:15:12.128
Wrong place, wrong time.

00:15:12.131 --> 00:15:14.603
I thought you were gonna toss
me some cheap pickup line.

00:15:14.608 --> 00:15:18.060
Most hunters come through that door,
think they can get in my pants with some

00:15:18.575 --> 00:15:21.685
Pizza, a six-Pack and
side one of "Zeppelin 4".

00:15:23.014 --> 00:15:24.812
What a bunch of scumbags.

00:15:26.328 --> 00:15:27.589
Not you.

00:15:28.834 --> 00:15:30.112
I guess not.

00:15:32.103 --> 00:15:33.651
Dean, come here. Check this out.

00:15:35.279 --> 00:15:36.263
Yeah.

00:15:37.333 --> 00:15:41.136
A few murders not far from
here that Ellen caught wind of.

00:15:41.138 --> 00:15:43.029
Looks to me like there might be a hunt.

00:15:43.032 --> 00:15:45.364
Yeah, so? So,

00:15:45.368 --> 00:15:46.874
I told her we'd check it out.

00:15:48.154 --> 00:15:50.501
You got to be kidding me. Killer clown?

00:15:50.506 --> 00:15:53.758
Yeah, he left the daughter
unharmed and killed the parents.

00:15:53.763 --> 00:15:55.231
Ripped them to pieces, actually.

00:15:55.237 --> 00:15:57.275
And this family was at
some carnival that night?

00:15:57.283 --> 00:15:59.912
Right, the Cooper carnival.

00:15:59.915 --> 00:16:02.716
How do you know we're not dealing
with some psycho carny in a clown suit?

00:16:02.721 --> 00:16:07.125
The cops have no leads, and all the
employees were tearing down shop...

00:16:07.131 --> 00:16:11.142
Alibis all around. Plus the girl said
she saw a clown vanish into thin air.

00:16:11.149 --> 00:16:14.591
Cops are saying trauma, of course.
I know what you're thinking, Sam.

00:16:14.597 --> 00:16:16.714
"Why did it have to be clowns?"

00:16:17.191 --> 00:16:18.570
Oh, give me a break.

00:16:18.573 --> 00:16:20.271
You didn't think I remembered, did you?

00:16:21.129 --> 00:16:25.002
Come on, you still bust out crying whenever
you see Ronald Mcdonald on the television.

00:16:25.015 --> 00:16:26.353
At least I'm not afraid of flying.

00:16:26.359 --> 00:16:28.848
Planes crash! And
apparently clowns kill.

00:16:32.672 --> 00:16:34.793
So, these types of murders,
they ever happen before?

00:16:35.348 --> 00:16:38.537
Uh, according to the file, 1981, the

00:16:38.543 --> 00:16:41.123
Bunker Brothers Circus.

00:16:41.128 --> 00:16:45.100
Same m.O. It happened three different
times, three different locales.

00:16:45.106 --> 00:16:49.562
It's weird though. If it is a spirit, it's usually
bound to a specific locale. A house or a town.

00:16:49.564 --> 00:16:52.235
How's this one moving from city
to city? Carnival to carnival?

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:53.520
Cursed object, maybe.

00:16:53.803 --> 00:16:56.264
Spirit attaches itself
to something, and the

00:16:56.270 --> 00:17:00.372
Carnival carries it around.
Great. Paranormal scavenger hunt.

00:17:01.150 --> 00:17:03.169
This case was your idea.

00:17:03.174 --> 00:17:06.725
By the way, why is that? You were
awfully quick to jump on this job.

00:17:07.761 --> 00:17:10.050
So? So this is not like you, that's all.

00:17:10.578 --> 00:17:13.527
I thought you were hell-Bent
for leather on the demon hunt.

00:17:14.647 --> 00:17:15.964
I don't know. I just think

00:17:15.978 --> 00:17:18.851
Taking this job, it's what
dad would have wanted us to do.

00:17:19.294 --> 00:17:21.656
What dad would have wanted? Yeah.

00:17:22.984 --> 00:17:23.988
So?

00:17:28.052 --> 00:17:28.991
Nothing.

00:17:36.529 --> 00:17:37.745
Check it out.

00:17:41.100 --> 00:17:42.165
Evan, look.

00:17:43.302 --> 00:17:46.694
Scary! Yeah, dad, scary.

00:17:46.701 --> 00:17:47.698
What's over here?

00:17:54.115 --> 00:17:57.124
You know, when I was your age, this
would have scared the pants off me.

00:18:20.506 --> 00:18:21.496
Evan.

00:18:21.809 --> 00:18:22.627
Hey.

00:18:24.276 --> 00:18:25.192
What is it?

00:18:26.930 --> 00:18:28.167
I...

00:18:28.544 --> 00:18:29.932
I saw a clown.

00:18:32.292 --> 00:18:33.797
Don't be afraid of clowns.

00:18:34.115 --> 00:18:36.456
They're nice. They're your friends.

00:18:36.469 --> 00:18:38.659
Okay? Come on.

00:18:51.870 --> 00:18:52.896
Dad.

00:18:54.786 --> 00:18:55.773
Dad!

00:18:57.722 --> 00:18:58.570
Evan.

00:18:58.893 --> 00:18:59.942
What is it?

00:19:00.428 --> 00:19:02.156
You were right.

00:19:02.620 --> 00:19:04.151
He is my friend.

00:19:30.557 --> 00:19:31.574
Check it out.

00:19:31.581 --> 00:19:32.565
Five-O.

00:19:57.192 --> 00:19:58.117
Did you get her number?

00:20:02.670 --> 00:20:05.029
More murders? Two more last night.

00:20:05.035 --> 00:20:06.565
Apparently, they were ripped to shreds,

00:20:06.568 --> 00:20:08.366
And they had a little boy with them.

00:20:08.382 --> 00:20:10.099
Who fingered a clown.

00:20:14.134 --> 00:20:14.960
W hat?

00:20:15.608 --> 00:20:18.198
Yes, a clown, who apparently
vanished into thin air.

00:20:18.655 --> 00:20:21.212
Dean, you know, looking for
a cursed object, it's like

00:20:21.738 --> 00:20:24.759
Trying to find a needle in a stack
of needles. It could be anything.

00:20:25.625 --> 00:20:28.900
Well, it's bound to give off emf. So
we'll just have to scan everything.

00:20:28.902 --> 00:20:33.296
Oh, good. That's nice and inconspicuous.

00:20:33.544 --> 00:20:35.581
I guess we'll just have to blend in.

00:20:47.450 --> 00:20:48.479
Excuse me.

00:20:48.824 --> 00:20:50.922
We're looking for a Mr. Cooper.
Have you seen him around?

00:20:51.378 --> 00:20:53.125
What is that? Some kind of joke?

00:20:57.018 --> 00:20:59.288
Oh, god, I'm sorry. You think
I wouldn't give my eyeteeth

00:20:59.294 --> 00:21:03.917
To see Mr. Cooper or a
sunset or anything at all?

00:21:03.924 --> 00:21:05.190
Want to give me a little help here?

00:21:05.197 --> 00:21:06.151
Not really.

00:21:06.157 --> 00:21:08.165
Hey, Barry, is there a problem?

00:21:09.454 --> 00:21:13.115
Yeah, this guy hates
blind people. No, I don't.

00:21:13.120 --> 00:21:16.243
Hey, buddy, what's your problem? Nothing.
It's just a little misunderstanding.

00:21:16.249 --> 00:21:17.257
Little?

00:21:17.270 --> 00:21:19.218
You son of a bitch. No, no, no!

00:21:19.232 --> 00:21:21.595
Could somebody tell
me where Mr. Cooper is?

00:21:22.149 --> 00:21:23.347
Please?

00:21:23.353 --> 00:21:25.520
You boys picked a hell
of a time to join up.

00:21:25.715 --> 00:21:27.034
Take a seat.

00:21:27.592 --> 00:21:30.161
We got all kinds of local trouble.

00:21:31.939 --> 00:21:33.215
What do you mean?

00:21:33.314 --> 00:21:37.467
A couple of folks got themselves murdered.
Cops always seem to start here first.

00:21:37.472 --> 00:21:40.131
So, you two ever work
the circuit before?

00:21:40.134 --> 00:21:43.437
Uh, yes, sir. Last year
through Texas and Arkansas.

00:21:43.441 --> 00:21:45.079
Doing what?

00:21:45.787 --> 00:21:46.916
Ride jockeys?

00:21:47.332 --> 00:21:48.349
Pull shoot?

00:21:49.204 --> 00:21:51.243
A-And-S men?
Yeah, it's a...

00:21:51.497 --> 00:21:53.055
Little bit of everything, I guess.

00:21:55.747 --> 00:21:58.967
You two have never worked a show
in your lives before, have you?

00:22:00.204 --> 00:22:01.084
Nope.

00:22:02.060 --> 00:22:03.336
But we really need the work.

00:22:05.316 --> 00:22:07.427
And Sam here's got a
thing for the bearded lady.

00:22:12.230 --> 00:22:13.266
You see that picture?

00:22:14.453 --> 00:22:15.470
That's my daddy.

00:22:15.986 --> 00:22:17.024
You look just like him.

00:22:17.200 --> 00:22:18.487
He was in the business.

00:22:19.275 --> 00:22:22.175
Ran a freak show 'til they
outlawed them most places.

00:22:22.401 --> 00:22:25.911
Apparently displaying the
deformed isn't dignified.

00:22:25.917 --> 00:22:29.359
So, most of the performers went
from honest work to rotting in

00:22:29.365 --> 00:22:31.313
Hospitals and asylums.

00:22:32.609 --> 00:22:33.837
That's progress,

00:22:34.392 --> 00:22:35.361
I guess.

00:22:37.879 --> 00:22:39.228
You see, this place

00:22:39.303 --> 00:22:41.163
Is a refuge for outcasts.

00:22:41.328 --> 00:22:42.596
Always has been.

00:22:42.882 --> 00:22:45.180
For folks that don't
fit in nowhere else.

00:22:47.081 --> 00:22:47.995
But you two...

00:22:50.157 --> 00:22:51.875
You should go to school,

00:22:52.529 --> 00:22:53.828
Find a couple of girls,

00:22:54.125 --> 00:22:56.102
Have 2.5 kids,

00:22:56.108 --> 00:22:57.657
Live regular.

00:23:02.261 --> 00:23:03.188
Sir...

00:23:05.537 --> 00:23:06.734
We don't want to go to school.

00:23:07.158 --> 00:23:08.836
And we don't want regular.

00:23:09.595 --> 00:23:10.984
We want this.

00:23:15.014 --> 00:23:16.084
What?

00:23:17.430 --> 00:23:20.300
That whole "I don't want
to go back to school" thing,

00:23:20.505 --> 00:23:21.312
You just...

00:23:22.051 --> 00:23:24.290
You were just saying that
to Cooper, or were you,

00:23:24.636 --> 00:23:25.550
You know,

00:23:25.555 --> 00:23:26.473
Saying it?

00:23:28.473 --> 00:23:30.241
I don't know. You don't know?

00:23:31.257 --> 00:23:33.398
I thought that once the demon was dead

00:23:33.403 --> 00:23:36.602
And the fat lady sings that you were
gonna take off, head back to wussy state.

00:23:37.058 --> 00:23:38.387
I'm having second thoughts.

00:23:39.021 --> 00:23:40.800
Really? Yeah, I think...

00:23:42.632 --> 00:23:44.248
Dad would have wanted
me to stick to the job.

00:23:44.255 --> 00:23:46.081
Since when do you give
a damn what dad wanted?

00:23:46.509 --> 00:23:48.706
You spent half your life doing
exactly what he didn't want.

00:23:48.723 --> 00:23:50.471
Since he died, okay?

00:23:52.361 --> 00:23:53.839
You have a problem with that?

00:23:57.230 --> 00:23:58.628
No, I don't have a problem at all.

00:25:01.848 --> 00:25:02.946
Who is this?

00:25:40.796 --> 00:25:42.273
Hello? Hey, man.

00:25:43.069 --> 00:25:44.979
What's the matter? You sound
like you just saw a clown.

00:25:45.685 --> 00:25:46.653
Very funny.

00:25:48.740 --> 00:25:50.078
Skeleton, actually.

00:25:51.227 --> 00:25:53.626
Like a real human
skeleton? In the fun house.

00:25:53.632 --> 00:25:55.139
Listen, I was thinking. What if

00:25:55.145 --> 00:25:58.275
The spirit isn't attached to a cursed object.
What if it's attached to its own remains.

00:25:58.280 --> 00:26:00.639
Did the bones give off
emf? Well, no, but...

00:26:00.646 --> 00:26:02.686
We should check it out
anyway. I'm heading to you.

00:26:05.136 --> 00:26:07.424
What are you doing here, kid?

00:26:08.702 --> 00:26:11.033
Just sweeping. Bull.

00:26:11.035 --> 00:26:13.816
And what were you
talking about? Skeletons?

00:26:13.822 --> 00:26:15.472
What's emf?

00:26:16.567 --> 00:26:18.857
Dude, your blind-Man
hearing is out of control.

00:26:18.863 --> 00:26:21.041
We're a tight-Knit group.
We don't like outsiders.

00:26:21.046 --> 00:26:23.505
We take care of our own problems.

00:26:24.432 --> 00:26:26.632
We got a problem? You
tell me. You're the one

00:26:26.638 --> 00:26:29.018
Talking about human bones.

00:26:31.998 --> 00:26:33.307
Do you believe in ghosts?

00:26:33.902 --> 00:26:34.679
What?

00:26:34.853 --> 00:26:35.961
My brother and me...

00:26:38.011 --> 00:26:39.326
We're writing a book about them.

00:26:42.390 --> 00:26:44.146
What took you so long? Long story.

00:26:44.152 --> 00:26:46.132
Mommy, look at the clown.

00:26:48.632 --> 00:26:49.770
What clown?

00:26:54.301 --> 00:26:56.041
Come on, sweetie. Come on.

00:27:10.233 --> 00:27:11.714
Dean, I cannot believe

00:27:11.718 --> 00:27:14.049
You told Papasian about
the homicidal phantom clown.

00:27:14.052 --> 00:27:16.961
I told him an urban legend
about a homicidal phantom clown.

00:27:16.966 --> 00:27:18.377
I never said it was real. Keep it down.

00:27:20.587 --> 00:27:21.761
Oh, and get this.

00:27:21.769 --> 00:27:23.935
I mentioned the Bunker
Brothers Circus in '81

00:27:24.022 --> 00:27:26.921
And their evil-Clown
apocalypse. Guess what.

00:27:26.926 --> 00:27:27.716
What?

00:27:28.339 --> 00:27:30.359
Before Mr. Cooper owned Cooper carnival,

00:27:30.816 --> 00:27:32.204
He worked for the Bunker Brothers.

00:27:32.209 --> 00:27:33.405
He was their lot manager.

00:27:33.412 --> 00:27:35.328
So you think whatever's
the spirit attached to

00:27:35.346 --> 00:27:37.825
Cooper just brought it with
him? Something like that.

00:27:40.546 --> 00:27:42.643
I can't believe we keep
talking about clowns.

00:28:10.764 --> 00:28:12.724
Want to come in and play?

00:28:27.368 --> 00:28:30.760
Want to see mommy and
daddy? They're upstairs.

00:28:32.709 --> 00:28:33.808
Hey!

00:28:43.482 --> 00:28:45.190
Sam, watch out!

00:28:49.621 --> 00:28:51.243
What's going on in here?

00:28:51.248 --> 00:28:53.505
Oh, my god! What do you do to my
daughter! Get away from my kid!

00:28:53.509 --> 00:28:56.482
Mommy, daddy, they shot my clown.

00:29:07.017 --> 00:29:08.566
You really think they saw our plates?

00:29:10.364 --> 00:29:11.873
I don't want to take the chance.

00:29:12.049 --> 00:29:14.077
Besides, I hate this
freaking thing anyway.

00:29:16.235 --> 00:29:17.896
Well, one thing's for sure.

00:29:17.898 --> 00:29:18.886
What's that?

00:29:19.662 --> 00:29:21.090
We're not dealing with a spirit.

00:29:21.416 --> 00:29:23.193
That rock salt hit something solid.

00:29:23.392 --> 00:29:27.011
Yeah, a person, or maybe a creature
that can make itself invisible?

00:29:27.026 --> 00:29:29.035
Yeah, and dresses up
like a clown for kicks?

00:29:29.040 --> 00:29:30.478
Did it say anything in dad's journal?

00:29:30.495 --> 00:29:31.190
Nope.

00:29:34.785 --> 00:29:35.558
Who you calling?

00:29:35.984 --> 00:29:38.526
Maybe Ellen or that guy
Ash will know something.

00:29:39.291 --> 00:29:40.970
Hey, you think, uh...

00:29:41.568 --> 00:29:43.537
You think dad and
Ellen ever had a thing?

00:29:43.843 --> 00:29:44.770
No way.

00:29:45.062 --> 00:29:46.842
Then why didn't he tell us about her?

00:29:47.227 --> 00:29:49.306
I don't know. Maybe they
had some sort of falling-Out.

00:29:50.235 --> 00:29:51.099
Yeah.

00:29:53.452 --> 00:29:56.090
You ever notice dad had a
falling-Out with just about everybody?

00:30:00.837 --> 00:30:02.464
Don't get all maudlin on me, man.

00:30:02.467 --> 00:30:03.296
What do you mean?

00:30:03.902 --> 00:30:07.722
I mean this strong, silent thing
of yours. It's crap. I'm over it.

00:30:07.727 --> 00:30:10.010
This isn't just anyone we're
talking about. This is dad.

00:30:10.013 --> 00:30:11.733
I know how you felt about the man.

00:30:11.735 --> 00:30:14.928
Back off, all right? Just because I'm
not caring and sharing like you want...

00:30:14.932 --> 00:30:17.876
No, no, no. That's not what this is about,
Dean. I don't care how you deal with this,

00:30:17.878 --> 00:30:19.666
But you have to deal with it, man.

00:30:21.175 --> 00:30:23.484
Listen, I'm your brother, all right?
I just want to make sure you're okay.

00:30:23.492 --> 00:30:25.380
Dude, I'm okay! I'm okay!

00:30:25.385 --> 00:30:27.494
I swear, the next person
who asks me if I'm okay,

00:30:27.498 --> 00:30:29.005
I'm gonna start throwing punches.

00:30:29.200 --> 00:30:31.523
These are your issues.
Quit dumping them on me.

00:30:31.525 --> 00:30:32.472
What are you talking about?

00:30:32.487 --> 00:30:35.319
I just think it's really interesting
this sudden obedience you have to dad.

00:30:35.323 --> 00:30:37.184
It's like, "oh, what
would dad want me to do?"

00:30:37.567 --> 00:30:39.998
You spent your entire life
slugging it out with that man.

00:30:40.004 --> 00:30:42.632
I mean, hell, you picked a fight with
him the last time you ever saw him,

00:30:42.638 --> 00:30:44.677
And now that he's dead,
now you wanna make it right?

00:30:44.681 --> 00:30:47.243
Well, I'm sorry, Sam, but you
can't. It's too little too late.

00:30:47.247 --> 00:30:48.397
Why are you saying this to me?

00:30:48.401 --> 00:30:52.162
I want you to be honest with yourself
about this! I'm dealing with dad's death.

00:30:52.637 --> 00:30:53.536
Are you?

00:30:59.413 --> 00:31:00.479
I'm gonna call Ellen.

00:31:12.278 --> 00:31:13.375
Thanks a lot.

00:31:15.564 --> 00:31:16.851
Rakshasa.

00:31:17.459 --> 00:31:19.808
What's that? Ellen's best guess.

00:31:20.154 --> 00:31:23.835
It's a race of ancient hindu
creatures. They appear in human form,

00:31:23.842 --> 00:31:25.801
They feed on human flesh,

00:31:26.116 --> 00:31:27.814
They can make themselves invisible,

00:31:27.818 --> 00:31:30.599
And they cannot enter a home
without first being invited to.

00:31:30.604 --> 00:31:33.154
They dress up like clowns,
and children invite them in.

00:31:33.159 --> 00:31:35.420
Why don't they just munch
on the kids? No idea.

00:31:35.606 --> 00:31:37.073
Not enough meat on the bones, maybe?

00:31:37.077 --> 00:31:40.420
What else you find out? Apparently,
rakshasas live in squalor.

00:31:40.793 --> 00:31:43.494
They sleep on a bed of dead insects.

00:31:44.393 --> 00:31:47.194
And they have to feed a few
times. Every 20 to 30 years.

00:31:47.198 --> 00:31:49.616
Slow metabolism, I
guess. That makes sense.

00:31:49.622 --> 00:31:52.622
The carnival today, the
Bunker Brothers in '81.

00:31:52.630 --> 00:31:54.887
Probably more before that.

00:31:55.092 --> 00:31:57.231
Sam, who do we know
that worked both shows?

00:31:57.236 --> 00:31:58.905
Cooper? Cooper.

00:32:00.245 --> 00:32:02.111
You know, that picture of his father,

00:32:02.379 --> 00:32:03.604
That looked just like him.

00:32:04.543 --> 00:32:05.880
You think maybe it was him?

00:32:06.767 --> 00:32:08.526
Well, who knows how old he is?

00:32:08.530 --> 00:32:09.847
Ellen say how to kill him?

00:32:10.332 --> 00:32:13.353
Legend goes a dagger made of pure brass.

00:32:15.404 --> 00:32:17.314
I think I know where
to get one of those.

00:32:17.318 --> 00:32:20.528
Well, before we go stabbing things into Cooper,
we're gonna want to make damn sure it's him.

00:32:20.534 --> 00:32:23.216
Oh, you're such a stickler
for details, Sammy.

00:32:23.910 --> 00:32:25.710
All right, I'll round up the blade.

00:32:25.956 --> 00:32:28.092
You go check if Cooper's got bedbugs.

00:32:49.713 --> 00:32:52.263
Well, I got all kinds of knives.

00:32:52.556 --> 00:32:55.106
I don't know if I got
a brass one, though.

00:33:03.800 --> 00:33:04.916
What do you think you're doing?

00:33:07.239 --> 00:33:08.524
Check the trunk.

00:33:25.443 --> 00:33:26.312
You?

00:33:30.573 --> 00:33:31.680
Me.

00:33:45.262 --> 00:33:46.370
All right!

00:33:47.656 --> 00:33:48.864
Jeez.

00:33:51.085 --> 00:33:52.090
Hey!

00:33:52.768 --> 00:33:53.554
Hey!

00:33:54.441 --> 00:33:57.132
So, Cooper thinks I'm a
peeping tom, but it's not him.

00:33:57.136 --> 00:33:58.384
Yeah, so I gathered.

00:33:58.401 --> 00:34:00.128
It's the blind guy. He's here somewhere.

00:34:00.132 --> 00:34:02.313
Well, did you get...
The brass blades? No.

00:34:02.319 --> 00:34:03.874
It's just been one of those days.

00:34:05.142 --> 00:34:06.801
I got an idea. Come on.

00:34:18.441 --> 00:34:20.209
Dean, find the maze, okay?

00:35:00.201 --> 00:35:01.138
Where is it? I don't know.

00:35:01.144 --> 00:35:02.882
Shouldn't we see his
clothes walking around?

00:35:17.788 --> 00:35:19.788
Dean, where is it? I don't know!

00:35:34.121 --> 00:35:36.388
Sam, behind you!

00:36:03.399 --> 00:36:05.006
I hate fun houses.

00:36:20.374 --> 00:36:21.842
You boys did a hell of a job.

00:36:22.007 --> 00:36:23.873
Your dad would be proud. Thanks.

00:36:32.669 --> 00:36:34.847
Oh, yeah, I've got to, uh...

00:36:36.647 --> 00:36:37.942
I've got to go...

00:36:38.379 --> 00:36:39.618
Over there...

00:36:39.900 --> 00:36:41.159
Right now.

00:36:46.063 --> 00:36:47.911
So. So.

00:36:49.519 --> 00:36:50.798
Am I gonna see you again?

00:36:53.698 --> 00:36:54.818
Do you want to?

00:36:56.874 --> 00:36:58.132
I wouldn't hate it.

00:36:58.939 --> 00:37:00.178
Can I be honest with you?

00:37:00.473 --> 00:37:01.590
See, normally,

00:37:01.594 --> 00:37:04.126
I'd be hitting on you so
fast it'd make your head spin.

00:37:04.492 --> 00:37:05.519
But

00:37:06.984 --> 00:37:08.183
These days...

00:37:09.350 --> 00:37:10.179
I don't know.

00:37:10.745 --> 00:37:11.822
Wrong place,

00:37:12.555 --> 00:37:13.913
Wrong time?

00:37:15.503 --> 00:37:16.779
It's okay. I get it.

00:37:20.123 --> 00:37:22.120
Where you guys been?

00:37:22.267 --> 00:37:25.236
I've been waiting for you.
We were working a job, Ash.

00:37:26.556 --> 00:37:28.845
Clowns? Clowns? What the...

00:37:28.851 --> 00:37:30.037
You got something for us, Ash?

00:37:30.954 --> 00:37:32.361
Did you find the demon?

00:37:32.575 --> 00:37:33.774
It's nowhere around,

00:37:33.978 --> 00:37:35.696
At least nowhere I can find.

00:37:35.713 --> 00:37:38.472
But if this fugly
bastard raises its head,

00:37:38.971 --> 00:37:42.744
I'll know. I mean, I'm on
it like divine on dog dookie.

00:37:42.746 --> 00:37:43.684
What do you mean?

00:37:44.472 --> 00:37:45.717
I mean

00:37:46.446 --> 00:37:49.605
Any of those signs or omens
appear anywhere in the world,

00:37:49.609 --> 00:37:52.472
My rig will go off like a fire alarm.

00:37:53.347 --> 00:37:54.456
You mind?

00:37:58.898 --> 00:37:59.927
What's up, man?

00:38:01.897 --> 00:38:03.764
Ash, where did you learn to do all this?

00:38:03.771 --> 00:38:07.903
M.I.T., before I got
bounced for fighting.

00:38:10.171 --> 00:38:11.150
M.I.T.?

00:38:11.423 --> 00:38:12.801
It's a school in Boston.

00:38:13.708 --> 00:38:14.515
Okay.

00:38:15.120 --> 00:38:16.671
Give us a call as soon
as you know something?

00:38:17.254 --> 00:38:18.946
S, s, compadre.

00:38:30.121 --> 00:38:31.479
Hey, listen.

00:38:32.315 --> 00:38:35.275
If you boys need a place to stay,
I got a couple beds out back.

00:38:36.795 --> 00:38:37.921
Thanks, but no.

00:38:39.130 --> 00:38:40.737
There's something I got to finish.

00:38:40.744 --> 00:38:41.571
Okay.

00:38:56.916 --> 00:38:57.792
You were right.

00:38:59.331 --> 00:39:00.217
About what?

00:39:04.891 --> 00:39:05.948
About me and dad.

00:39:06.936 --> 00:39:09.847
I'm sorry that the last time I was
with him, I tried to pick a fight.

00:39:10.282 --> 00:39:12.660
I'm sorry that I spent most
of my life angry at him.

00:39:12.807 --> 00:39:14.516
I mean, for all I know, he died

00:39:14.642 --> 00:39:15.977
Thinking that I hate him.

00:39:18.177 --> 00:39:19.335
So, you're right.

00:39:21.486 --> 00:39:23.685
What I'm doing right
now... It is too little.

00:39:25.892 --> 00:39:26.891
It's too late.

00:39:32.347 --> 00:39:33.753
I miss him, man.

00:39:36.724 --> 00:39:38.332
And I feel guilty as hell.

00:39:42.224 --> 00:39:43.604
And I'm not all right...

00:39:45.672 --> 00:39:46.729
Not at all...

00:39:55.480 --> 00:39:56.678
But neither are you.

00:39:58.467 --> 00:39:59.537
That much I know.

00:40:03.887 --> 00:40:05.368
I'll let you get back to work.

00:00:13.481 --> 00:00:14.984
<font color="#ffff00" size=14>www.tvsubtitles.net</font>
